\b PARTRACEFLOW MES END-TO-END GUIDE\b0\par
\par
This document consolidates the MES walkthrough into one document-style file for the docs folder. It is intended to be opened directly in Microsoft Word or any editor that supports RTF.\par
\par
\b 1. Purpose\b0\par
ParTraceflow MES is a full-stack manufacturing execution system for production tracking, quality control, traceability, machine monitoring, shift operations, workflows, and pipe spool management.\par
\par
\b 2. Before You Start\b0\par
1. Install Node.js 18 or later.\par
2. Open a terminal in the project root.\par
3. Change into the app folder.\par
4. Ensure the environment file contains a valid database URL and session secret.\par
\par
\f1
cd .\mes-app
\par
npm install
\par
npx prisma generate
\par
npx prisma db push
\par
npx prisma db seed
\par
npm run dev
\f0
\par
\par
\b 3. Open The System\b0\par
Open http://localhost:3000 in the browser.\par
\par
\b 4. Log In\b0\par
Use one of the seeded demo accounts. Example accounts commonly used in this project are:\par
1. admin / admin123\par
2. SUPV-LEE / demo\par
3. QC-SARAH / demo\par
