5. OP-MARIA / demo\par
\par
\b 5. Main Navigation Flow\b0\par
The core end-to-end walkthrough of the MES should be followed in this order:\par
1. Dashboard\par
2. Planner\par
3. Operator\par
4. Quality\par
5. Traceability\par
6. Andon and factory monitoring\par
7. Pipe spool workflow\par
8. Admin and workflow configuration\par
\par
\b 6. Dashboard Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the dashboard page.\par
2. Review overall KPIs such as production, downtime, and OEE.\par
3. Confirm live machine or line status indicators are visible.\par
4. Check active alerts and event summaries.\par
5. Use the dashboard as the supervisor entry point before moving into detailed execution pages.\par
\par
\b 7. Production Planning Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the planner page.\par
2. Review work orders, priorities, due dates, and scheduling information.\par
3. Verify production resources and machine assignments.\par
4. Confirm the next work order that should be executed on the shop floor.\par
5. Move to the operator page to execute production.\par
\par
\b 8. Operator Execution Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the operator page.\par
2. Select the assigned work order or queued job.\par
3. Start the job or task.\par
4. Record progress, output, and any downtime reason if an interruption occurs.\par
5. Complete the task when the operation finishes.\par
6. Confirm the system updates status and feeds downstream quality and traceability records.\par
\par
\b 9. Quality Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the quality page.\par
2. Review inspection queues, quality alerts, and SPC views.\par
3. Record inspection results.\par
4. Approve accepted items or raise NCRs when issues are found.\par
5. Verify that the quality decision updates the product or spool lifecycle correctly.\par
\par
\b 10. Traceability Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the traceability page or related traceability APIs.\par
2. Search by batch, lot, serial number, RFID tag, or spool identifier.\par
3. Confirm backward traceability to material source.\par
4. Confirm forward traceability to downstream assemblies or finished items.\par
5. Verify the audit trail contains production and quality events captured earlier.\par
\par
\b 11. Andon And Factory Monitoring Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open the andon page or factory map.\par
2. Review machine states, active issues, and operator-visible alerts.\par
3. Trigger or inspect a downtime event.\par
4. Confirm the alert appears in the dashboard and event stream.\par
5. Resolve the issue and verify the status returns to normal.\par
\par
\b 12. Pipe Spool End-To-End Walkthrough\b0\par
This is the most structured lifecycle in the system.\par
\par
Spool lifecycle:\par
FABRICATING -> RECEIVED -> IN_STORAGE -> ISSUED -> FIT_UP -> WELDED -> NDE_PENDING -> NDE_CLEAR -> PRESSURE_TESTED -> COMPLETE\par
\par
Follow these steps:\par
1. Create or open a spool record.\par
2. Confirm material receipt and spool registration.\par
3. Move the spool into storage.\par
4. Issue the spool for work.\par
5. Record fit-up activities.\par
6. Record welding details including welder and procedure references.\par
7. Create NDE records and submit them for review.\par
8. If the NDE passes, advance to NDE_CLEAR.\par
9. If the NDE fails, create or link NCR actions and resolve them.\par
10. Perform pressure testing and record the certificate or result.\par
11. Close all inspection and approval items.\par
12. Mark the spool complete when documentation is fully ready.\par
\par
\b 13. RFID Flow\b0\par
1. A reader or gateway posts a tag event to the MES.\par
2. The system receives the event through the RFID ingestion endpoint.\par
3. The event is deduplicated.\par
4. The spool or tracked item is identified.\par
5. The corresponding lifecycle or location update is applied.\par
6. Reader health can be checked through the reader status endpoint.\par
\par
\b 14. Workflow And Approval Flow\b0\par
1. Open the workflow designer.\par
2. Create or edit a process definition.\par
3. Define the steps, routing, and assigned roles.\par
4. Save the workflow.\par
5. Deploy the workflow.\par
6. Start a workflow instance from the relevant business context.\par
7. Complete tasks as each assigned role.\par
8. Confirm the workflow reaches completion and generates an audit trail.\par
\par
\b 15. Admin Walkthrough\b0\par
1. Open admin-facing pages or configuration areas.\par
2. Review user roles and permissions.\par
3. Confirm machine, product, workflow, and operational master data are valid.\par
4. Review event logs, notifications, and health endpoints.\par
5. Use admin tools only after the end-user operational flow has been validated.\par
\par
